; Sprites: flapper, left and right (8 frames); also Willy in The Nightmare Room
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B600+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. A small creature with a body and a flapping wing drawn in a dithered
; pattern. Frames 0-3 face left, 4-7 face right (the order of the entity pages: bit 7 of entity byte +0 selects the
; right half). Used by entity definition $1A in rooms $02 $0B $0C $27. #R$9637 also uses this page instead of Willy's
; own sprites (#R$9D00) in The Nightmare Room (room $1D): it XORs bit 7 of the frame offset, because Willy's sprites
; have the right-facing frames first while this page has the left-facing ones first.
@label=SpritesFlapper
b$B600 DEFB $00,$00 ; frame 0: flapper facing left, frame 0
